# The build context of Dockerfile.release (#361). BuildKit reads
# `<Dockerfile>.dockerignore` in preference to `.dockerignore`, which stays the
# dev image's: the dev image needs test/ in its context (the compose smoke
# gate's fixture), the release image must not have it. Generated by
# `mix phx.gen.release --docker`; what was added by hand is at the bottom.
#
# This file excludes paths from the Docker build context.
#
# By default, Docker's build context includes all files (and folders) in the
# current directory. Even if a file isn't copied into the container it is still sent to
# the Docker daemon.
#
# There are multiple reasons to exclude files from the build context:
#
# 1. Prevent nested folders from being copied into the container (ex: exclude
#    /assets/node_modules when copying /assets)
# 2. Reduce the size of the build context and improve build time (ex. /build, /deps, /doc)
# 3. Avoid sending files containing sensitive information
#
# More information on using .dockerignore is available here:
# https://docs.docker.com/engine/reference/builder/#dockerignore-file

.dockerignore

# Ignore git, but keep git HEAD and refs to access current commit hash if needed:
#
# $ cat .git/HEAD | awk '{print ".git/"$2}' | xargs cat
# d0b8727759e1e0e7aa3d41707d12376e373d5ecc
.git
!.git/HEAD
!.git/refs

# Common development/test artifacts
/cover/
/doc/
/test/
/tmp/
.elixir_ls

# Mix artifacts
/_build/
/deps/
*.ez

# Generated on crash by the VM
erl_crash.dump

# Static artifacts - These should be fetched and built inside the Docker image
# https://phoenix.hexdocs.pm/Mix.Tasks.Phx.Gen.Release.html#module-docker
/assets/node_modules/
/priv/static/assets/
/priv/static/cache_manifest.json

# --- Added by hand (#361) ---

# NIF binaries and cargo's build directory from the host. The parsebooks NIF
# is compiled in the builder stage and nowhere else, so a host-built .so can
# never reach the image.
/priv/native/
/native/parsebooks/target/

# The seeds create a login whose password is in the repo. The release never
# runs them, and cannot: the file is not in the image.
/priv/repo/seeds.exs

# Local secrets and the dev stack's environment.
.env
.env.*

# Dialyzer PLTs (large, machine-specific).
/priv/plts/

# Developer files a release has no use for: the reference documents loaded by
# CLAUDE.md's trigger table, and the git hooks `mix hooks.install` installs.
/priv/reference/
/priv/hooks/
